00:38:58.070 --> 00:38:58.880
It's a soft quota.

00:38:58.880 --> 00:39:01.040
So it's not-- like, if
you're running a database,

00:39:01.040 --> 00:39:04.560
you don't want it to stall
or corrupt the database.

00:39:04.560 --> 00:39:06.440
You want it to be
able to scale up.

00:39:06.440 --> 00:39:10.220
So it's a soft quota,
and it's more for you

00:39:10.220 --> 00:39:15.332
to manage and get the expected
performance out of that

00:39:15.332 --> 00:39:16.790
DEVIN LEHMAN: As
